+---
+id: task-003-apply-10-discount-to-rentals-of-3-days-in-quote-and-book
+type: task
+title: "Apply 10% discount to rentals of 3+ days in quote and book"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+A rental of 3 days or more now costs 10% less than its full price. Quotes and bookings both show the
+reduced total.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `applyLongStayDiscount(fullPrice, days)` in `src/index.ts`: for `days >= 3` it returns
+  `Math.round(fullPrice * 0.9)`, otherwise the full price unchanged.
+- Wired it into the shared `priceRequest` helper, so both `quote` and `book` return the discounted
+  total automatically (no duplicated logic between the two).
+- Test-first: added three failing tests (3-day quote discounted, 2-day quote undiscounted at the
+  boundary, rounding of a discount that doesn't land on a whole cent) plus one for `book`, confirmed
+  they failed against the pre-change code, then implemented until all 20 tests in
+  `test/rental-service.test.ts` pass (`node --test`).
+- Updated the `Quote.total`/`Booking.total` doc comments in `src/index.ts` and added a rule to
+  `README.md` describing the discount and that it is rounded to the nearest cent.
+- Recorded the rounding rule and where the discount is applied as
+  `dl-002-long-stay-discount-10-off-total-at-3-days-rounded-to-nearest-cent` (submitted, pending
+  approval).
+
+## Notes
+
+No new dependency or booking/validation behaviour was touched beyond pricing; `availability` is
+unaffected since it does not compute a total.
